 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "bosch washer FD 9409 not draining. ive cleaned the filter already. what part do i need?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "You likely need a new drain pump, as the filter has already been cleaned. If the machine still does not drain after replacing the pump, you may also need to check the drain hose for blockages. From what you have described, the most likely cause is a kink or blockage in the drain hose or waste pipe. Is there still water sitting in the drum, and when it tries to drain can you hear the pump running or humming?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Yes there's water left in the drum and the pump hums but the water doesn't move. Hose behind looks ok, no kinks. So is it the pump then?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "[Heading: Likely cause: drain pump]\nIt could be the pump, but it might also be a blockage in the internal drain pipe or a faulty pressure switch. You would need to check for obstructions inside the machine before assuming the pump itself has failed. The checks point to the drain pump. I could not find a confirmed match for model FD 9409 in our parts catalogue, so check with the manufacturer or a parts supplier using the full model number, or ask an appliance engineer to fit it."
  }
 ],
